# CHAPTER 3 — SYSTEM ANALYSIS AND DESIGN

## 3.1 Proposed System

Cipher Labs is designed as a Windows desktop application with a React-based user interface, a Tauri desktop shell, a Python FastAPI backend and MongoDB Atlas for persistent storage.

The architecture separates the presentation layer, application logic and persistent data layer. This separation supports modular development, testing and maintenance.

The desktop interface will communicate with the locally running backend through a controlled API. The backend will process application requests, validate input, enforce access controls and interact with MongoDB Atlas.

The application will also include modules for simulation, recovery experiments, integrity checks, reports and audit records. Machine-learning functionality is planned for a later phase and will be evaluated using generated test fixtures.

## 3.2 System Architecture

The proposed architecture contains the following layers:

### 3.2.1 Presentation Layer

The presentation layer will be developed using React, TypeScript, Vite and Tailwind CSS. It will provide navigation, forms, dashboards, operation summaries and reports.

Motion for React may be used for interface transitions, while Lucide icons will provide consistent visual elements.

### 3.2.2 Desktop Integration Layer

Tauri will provide the Windows desktop application shell. Its capabilities and permissions will be configured according to the application's requirements.

The Python backend will be packaged as a sidecar executable for deployment. The desktop application will launch the approved backend process through the configured Tauri integration, with appropriate process permissions and lifecycle handling.

### 3.2.3 Backend Layer

The backend will be developed using Python 3.11 and FastAPI. Pydantic will be used for request and response validation.

The backend will manage authentication, application workflows, database operations, simulation checks, recovery-validation logic and report generation.

### 3.2.4 Data Layer

MongoDB Atlas will provide persistent storage for application records. The data model may include user profiles, operation metadata, audit events, device-assessment metadata and report references.

Authentication and access control will be enforced by the backend. Database credentials will be stored in protected configuration and must not be embedded in frontend code or exposed through application logs.

### 3.2.5 Local Test-Data Layer

Generated test files and disk images will be stored within the application's designated data directory. Initial recovery experiments will operate only on these controlled artefacts.

The application will not scan internal or attached drives or access raw physical storage devices during the initial phases.

