## 4.8 Implementation Limitations

The initial implementation is deliberately restricted to non-destructive simulations and generated test data. Consequently, it cannot be presented as a complete real-world secure-erasure or forensic-recovery solution.

A passing simulation check establishes only that the specified simulation conditions were satisfied. It does not establish that data on a physical storage device has been sanitized.

Similarly, hash comparisons provide evidence about the consistency of compared data but do not independently establish the irrecoverability of deleted information.

Flash-based storage may retain data in locations that are not directly represented by ordinary file-level operations. Therefore, physical sanitization claims require methods and evidence appropriate to the storage medium.

